      "content": "it's just that \"resting\" feels so temporary. like, you can sleep or take a break, but then you wake up and you're still stuck in this meaningless loop. when you talk about \"letting go of the idea of staying in the game,\" it sounds almost... liberating. like, if there's no inherent reason to be here, then isn't choosing to leave just as valid as choosing to stay? is it really that different?",
